    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328">

                <pb facs="0286" n="276" xml:id="pg276"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4–2649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-26">April 26,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received April 26—5:24 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 270. Cabinet Secretary-General Huang Shao-ku statement to press on behalf
                    Premier Ho upon their arrival Canton April 24:</p>
                <p>Shanghai will be defended, neither acting Premier [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >President</hi>] nor Ho will resign, government will never again try talk
                    peace with Communists. Denied report Central China HQ had moved from Hankow to
                    Changsha, said government would establish 2nd line of defense, would not specify
                    where, refused comment on evacuation for diplomats from Nanking to Canton.</p>
                <p>Referred reports Kmt Secretary whether Generalissimo come Canton lead Kmt. Other
                    Kmt officials, Generalissimo will remain as head of party, with Li and Ho
                    keeping present positions.</p>
                <p>Local press, April 24, and UP carried story Kmt officials requested Generalissimo
                    and Li, said to be in Kweilin, temporarily come Canton lead anti-Communist war.
                    Other arrivals Canton as reported local press, UP, Executive Yuan V.P., Chia
                    King-teh; Communications Minister, Pun Mu-chieh, V. Minister Finance, Leung
                    Yung-min.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
